        ],
        "text": "Oral argument began before the Supreme Court at 11:11\u202fa.m."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner, Mr. Dabney, argued that the Federal Circuit\u2019s jurisdiction may be overly expansive, potentially excluding regional circuits."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Chief Justice asked whether Congress intended patent law to be uniform."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Chief Justice also asked whether the Federal Circuit has jurisdiction over patent counterclaims or only compulsory counterclaims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice O'Connor, justice O\u2019Connor posed a question during the argument."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, a Justice questioned whether the appellate meaning of \u201carising under\u201d excludes counterclaims for original jurisdiction purposes."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Gowdey",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Gowdey stated that there has not been a patent ruling in the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Gowdey",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Gowdey, mr. Gowdey explained that a well\u2011pled patent counterclaim at the pleading stage could place appellate jurisdiction in the Federal Circuit under the Aerojet rule."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Dabney",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f500a1969ce2a7ec4eac69ca1b2a03fa8cce80d431dedaa5f84d129f17feed77",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f500a1969ce2-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Dabney argued that the respondent\u2019s position would require the Court to retreat from the Christianson precedent and adopt a special interpretation of the \u201carising under\u201d language."
      }
